/**
 * ============================================================================
 * eHapot Backend Engine
 * BISCAST Student Development Services
 * Version 2.4.1
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * ARCHITECTURE
 * Frontend: GitHub Pages / static HTML
 * Backend: Google Apps Script Web App
 * Database: Google Sheets
 *
 * SECURITY MODEL
 * 1. EVENT PIN
 *        - Public 4-6 digit session identifier.
 *        - May appear in audience/projector URLs.
 *        - NOT a moderator password.
 *
 * 2. MODERATOR_SECRET
 *        - Private credential stored only in Apps Script Script Properties.
 *        - Required for every moderator-only backend request.
 *
 * 3. ADMIN_SECRET (v2.4.1)
 *        - Separate, higher-tier credential, also Script-Properties-only.
 *        - Grants the raw Google Sheet link (QnA_Master / Audit_Log) via the
 *          'verifyAdmin' action. A moderator session alone does NOT expose
 *          this URL - the old public launchpad "View Audit Logs" card and
 *          the auto-shown Sheet link in the moderator dashboard were both
 *          removed for this exact reason (anyone with MODERATOR_SECRET
 *          previously got sheet-edit access for free).
 *        - If ADMIN_SECRET is not set, the action fails closed with a
 *          config error rather than silently granting access.
 *
 * OPTIONAL SCRIPT PROPERTY
 *        ACTIVE_EVENT_PIN
 *        - If set, only that event PIN is accepted.
 *        - If NOT set, any valid 4-6 digit event PIN is allowed.
 *        - This prevents a missing ACTIVE_EVENT_PIN from breaking the system.
 *
 * REQUIRED SCRIPT PROPERTIES
 *        MODERATOR_SECRET
 *        ADMIN_SECRET   (required only for the Admin Access / Audit Log
 *                         feature - the rest of eHapot works without it)
 *
 * DATABASE
 * QnA_Master:
 * ID | Timestamp | PIN | Question | Submitted_By | Status |
 * Moderator_Name | Mod_Timestamp | Rejection_Reason
 *
 * Audit_Log:
 * Timestamp | Actor | Action | Question_ID |
 * From_State | To_State | Meta
 *
 * Event_Settings (v2.4.0):
 * PIN | Setting_Key | Setting_Value | Updated_At | Updated_By
 * One row per (PIN, key) pair. Generic so future per-event settings
 * (e.g. an audience-size poll-interval toggle) can reuse the same sheet
 * without another schema change. Currently used for: eventTitle.
 * ============================================================================
 */

